{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Bugs and Debugging", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about bugs and debugging.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations. Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "defect ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an imperfection or problem in software programming", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What I see here is that while you are programming, you can find that actual results vary from expected results and there is an unwanted behavior. This is a bug also called defect or incident.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "spot ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to detect or identify an error in the system", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To spot these errors you need to check the flow or logic sequence of the program.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "symbol ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the different figures and marks used in software programming", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This error is in a language's rules for constructing statements or from using the wrong symbol like parentheses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "compile ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put information together in a document or text", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Since computer programs have to follow strict syntax to compile correctly, any aspect of the code that doesn't match the syntax of the programming language will constantly produce a syntax error.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "unexpected ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a result that was not the one someone expects", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The logic errors are defects that occur in a program's source code that results in incorrect or unexpected behavior.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "conduct ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to carry out an activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess defect prevention is very effective and efficient in reducing the number of bugs. That's why it's important to conduct defect discovery and removal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for information about bugs and how to avoid them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify different useful strategies in order to avoid them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a brochure presenting that information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the brochure with the class and discuss about it.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I search for information about bugs and how to avoid them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify different strategies useful for me in order to avoid them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a brochure presenting that information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the brochure with the class and discuss it.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "<div align=\"center\">Adverbs of Frequency, Usually, Constantly, Almost Always</div>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In English, we use the <strong>adverbs of frequency</strong> to mention how frequently we do an activity or action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <strong>adverbs</strong> can modify the meaning of a sentence by saying how often it happens. An <strong>adverb of frequency</strong> goes before the main verb of the sentence except the verb to be.</br></br>  For example:</br><i>A developer <strong>constantly</strong> finds bugs. </br> I <strong>almost always</strong> make mistakes when programming.</i></br></br>  When you use an auxiliary verb, the <strong>adverb</strong> goes in the middle of the auxiliary and the main verb.</br></br>   For example:</br><i>  Bugs  and defects in the system are <strong>usually</strong> prevented by running debugging.</i></br></br>Generally, the <strong>adverbs of frequency</strong> use a percentage to show the frequency. See the chart below.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>FREQUENCY</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>ADVERB</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">70 %</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">Constantly</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> 80 %</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">Usually</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> 90%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> Almost Always</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Most bugs are almost always due to human errors in source code or its design.      ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Since computer programs have to follow strict syntax to compile correctly, any aspect of the code that doesn't match the syntax of the programming language will constantly produce a syntax error. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Debugging is the process of finding and fixing bugs. The process usually starts after writing the code and continues in successive stages as code is combined with other units of programming.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "<div align=\"center\">Infinitives After Certain Verbs, Ask - Learn - Explain \u2013 Decide in Affirmative, Negative and Questions</div>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In English, if you need to write a verb with another action or activity, you usually use an <strong>infinitive</strong> following the main verb.  It allows you to express purpose in a sentence. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "After the following verbs : <span class=\"strong\">ask</span>, <span class=\"strong\">learn</span>, <span class=\"strong\">explain</span> and <span class=\"strong\">decide</span>, we always  have to use the infinitive form of another verb ( to+infinitive)  to introduce another action or activity.</br></br> Also, after the following verbs: <span class=\"strong\">advice</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ask</span>, <span class=\"strong\">encourage</span>, <span class=\"strong\">invite</span>, <span class=\"strong\">order</span>, <span class=\"strong\">persuade</span>, <span class=\"strong\">remind</span>, <span class=\"strong\">tell</span>, <span class=\"strong\">warn</span>, <span class=\"strong\">expect</span>, <span class=\"strong\">intend</span>, <span class=\"strong\">would prefer</span>, <span class=\"strong\">want</span>, <span class=\"strong\">would like</span>, we  can  use the infinitive form of another verb.</br></br>   <i>For example: </br> I am learning <strong>to</strong> detect bugs easier.</br> She decided <strong>to</strong> eliminate all the defects.</i></br></br>  If you want to create a sentence in negative, follow the next structure:</br></br> <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + main verb + (object) + verb in infinitive + complement</div>  </br></br>  <i>For example: </br> You asked her <strong>not</strong> to erase any bugs.</br> We decided <strong>not</strong> to update the system.</i></br></br>  In questions, use this:</br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\">(Wh word) + Aux. verb (Do-does-did) + subject + main verb + (object) + verb in infinitive + complement </div> </br></br>  <i>For example: </br>  Does she <span class=\"strong\">learn to program</span> applications?</br> Why do you <span class=\"strong\">ask him to leave</span> the platform?</i></br></br>   Look at the following chart:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Verb</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Infinitive</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">Ask</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ask to go, ask to leave\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">Learn</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Learn to create, learn to play\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">Explain</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explain to write, explain to update\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">Decide</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Decide to check, decide to get\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I'm having difficulties in this project. I try to finish with this programming language but I cannot. I decide not to continue until you can help me.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Can you explain me to identify logic errors? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sure. I am learning to identify them. For example, a syntax error is in the source code of a program.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can obtain information about bugs and debugging.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can explain different types of errors related to bugs and debugging.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify key features about bugs and debugging.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What are the most common problems a developer may find in software programming? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What information is necessary for a developer in order to understand and detect a software problem? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "g