"Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 12, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n2le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Grace:</strong> I'm having difficulties with this project. I'm trying to finish with this programming language but I couldn't. I decided not to continue until you can help me.</br>\n<strong>Scott:</strong> Thanks. What I see here is that while you are programming, you can find that actual results vary from expected results and there is an unwanted behavior. This is a bug also called defect or incident. Most bugs are almost always present due to human errors in source code or its design.\n</br><strong>Grace:</strong> I see what you mean.  I'm making mistakes during the process, right?</br>\n<strong>Scott:</strong> Yes, a bug is a coding error in a computer program. There are two main types of errors, syntax and logic errors. </br>", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "41200", "text": "<strong>Grace:</strong> I know what you mean, I am learning to identify them. For example, a syntax error is in the source code of a program. This error comes from the  language's rules for constructing statements or from using the wrong symbol like parentheses. </br><strong>Scott:</strong> Right. Since computer programs have to follow strict syntax to compile correctly, any aspect of the code that doesn't match the syntax of the programming language will constantly produce a syntax error.</br>\n<strong>Grace:</strong> Can you explain to me how to identify logic errors?</br>\n<strong>Scott:</strong> Well, the logic errors are defects that occur in a program's source code that results in incorrect or unexpected behavior. To spot these errors, you need to check the flow or logic sequence of the program.</br><strong>Grace:</strong> At college, my teacher asks me to learn about debugging.</br>", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "93000", "text": "<strong>Scott:</strong> Debugging is the process of finding and fixing bugs. The process usually starts after writing the code and continues in successive stages as code is combined with other units of programming.</br>\n<strong>Grace:</strong> I guess defect prevention is very effective and efficient in reducing the number of bugs. That's why it's important to conduct defect discovery and removal.", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n2le02ob03re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}